# Generated config trees (closed-model and open-model/Tinker). The declarative
# spec in experiments/open_models/make_configs.py is the source of truth; these
# .yaml trees are build artifacts. Regenerate all of them with:
#   python experiments/open_models/make_configs.py
# (add --checkpoints ckpts.json to bake Tinker LoRA paths into the open SFT arms)
# Ignore the generated *artifacts* (the .yaml files), NOT the directories:
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so a
# `configs/bigcodebench/` rule would make the hand-written plot_everything.sh
# below permanently un-addable once it is untracked.
src/lasr_labs_2025_control_project/configs/apps/**/*.yaml
src/lasr_labs_2025_control_project/configs/bigcodebench/**/*.yaml
src/lasr_labs_2025_control_project/configs/apps_open/**/*.yaml
src/lasr_labs_2025_control_project/configs/bigcodebench_open/**/*.yaml
# plot_everything.sh is hand-written and stays checked in under bigcodebench/;
# the copy mirrored into the open tree by the generator is an artifact.
src/lasr_labs_2025_control_project/configs/bigcodebench_open/plot_everything.sh
